# One line ending in the repository, decided here rather than by whichever
# machine last touched a file.
#
# This tree is written on Windows and its gate runs in WSL, so the same file
# was being checked out CRLF and committed LF, and `git status` printed a
# renormalisation warning on every second command. That is noise, and noise is
# how a real diff gets scrolled past. Git already stored LF in the index; this
# makes the checkout agree with it.
#
# `text=auto` lets git decide what is text and leaves binaries alone, which
# matters for the fixtures under tests/: a forced `text` on a .jsonl or a
# signed package would rewrite bytes that are hashed.
* text=auto eol=lf
